Each release attaches its Corresponding Source, whatsmeow-net_<version>_source.tar.gz, to the GitHub release whose tag is v followed by the package version, https://github.com/tcortega/Whatsmeow.NET/releases/tag/v<version>.
That archive holds the whole tagged repository plus the output of go mod vendor for sidecar/, the source of every module the binary links.
It builds without a network, with the Go toolchain that sidecar/go.mod names: in sidecar/, run CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=<os> GOARCH=<arch> go build -trimpath -ldflags "-s -w -X main.version=<version>" ./cmd/whatsmeow-net.
